## New Capabilities Identified

- **Generic wikilink scanning**: extract edges from `[[Page Name]]`/`[[Page Name|Alias]]` wikilinks anywhere in a page's Markdown body, retiring the current H2-heading-gated extractor (`extractWikilinks()` in `lib/frontmatter-parser.ts`), which only recognizes literal `## Related`/`## Referenced By` sections.
- **Title/filename-based link resolution**: resolve wikilinks against any note's filename or frontmatter title, case-insensitive, regardless of folder — replacing the current exact-slug-path match.
- **Embed exclusion**: recognize and exclude `![[Page Name]]` transclusion syntax from graph edges.
- **Graceful unresolved-link handling**: silently drop wikilinks with no matching note; log at DEBUG only.
- **Optional status field**: tolerate vaults with no `status` frontmatter; default affected nodes to a neutral/unknown status dot.
- **Normalized tag shapes**: accept `tags:` as a YAML array, comma/space-separated string, or inline `#hashtags`, unifying all into `tags: string[]`.

## Priority Signal

The user's stated priority is broadening vault-parsing to work against real-world Obsidian/PKM vaults, not just this project's own bespoke convention — a parsing-layer generalization, not a UI or feature change. Backward compatibility with the two existing deployed vaults (`second-brain`, `ai-adoption-wiki`) is a hard constraint, not a nice-to-have: their heading-scoped wikilinks must continue to produce the same edges without any vault migration, since the new full-body scan is a strict superset of the old H2-gated scan.

## Deferred Items

- Disambiguation UI for wikilinks resolving to multiple same-titled notes in different folders (resolved deterministically-but-silently for now)
- Support for Obsidian plugin-specific syntax: Dataview query blocks, Canvas `.canvas` files, Templater templates
- Support for other PKM tools' non-standard dialects: Logseq outline blocks, Roam block references
